            <ArticleTitle>Simultaneous two-vessel very-late stent thrombosis of everolimus-eluting stents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E48-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Very-late stent thrombosis is a rare complication. Several factors related to the patient, procedure, and premature discontinuation of antiplatelet therapy are known to contribute to its occurrence. This report describes the case of a 40-year-old patient with simultaneous two-vessel stent thrombosis (left anterior descending and right coronary arteries) 31 months after everolimus-eluting stent implantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
